---
import { Text } from "@/shared/ui/text";
---

<Text
  data-slot="site-footer-colophon"
  class="leading-relaxed"
  tone="faint"
  variant="small"
>
  Built with Astro and Tailwind CSS, with Alpine.js for the small interactive parts. Pages are prerendered and deployed
  on Vercel, apart from the books page, which is rendered on demand from my Hardcover library and cached for a few
  minutes. Posts and movies are files in the repository, edited through Keystatic. I chose static output and a little
  JavaScript over a client framework, and plain files in git over a database, so the site stays fast and easy to move.
  Covers and posters are resized by Astro for each screen density and fade in over a blurred preview. Code blocks use
  Expressive Code, math uses KaTeX, the code is organised with Feature-Sliced Design, and the type is Supreme, General
  Sans and Geist Mono.
</Text>
<Text
  data-slot="site-footer-attribution"
  class="leading-relaxed"
  tone="faint"
  variant="small"
>
  Book data and covers come from
  <a
    class="underline underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-foreground"
    href="https://hardcover.app"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    target="_blank"
  >
    Hardcover
  </a>
  , and film and series posters from
  <a
    class="underline underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-foreground"
    href="https://www.themoviedb.org"
    rel="noopener noreferrer"
    target="_blank"
  >
    TMDB
  </a>
  . This product uses the TMDB API but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB.
</Text>
